    answer: 'A formal dispute letter should include: your full name, date of birth, account number, date of service, Medicare or insurance ID number, a specific list of the disputed line items with their CPT codes and amounts, a clear statement of why each charge is being disputed (duplicate, unrendered service, upcoding, No Surprises Act violation), a request for a written response within 30 days, and your mailing address for the response. Send by certified mail with return receipt and keep a copy of everything.',
