  },
  {
    question: 'How long do I have to dispute a medical bill?',
    answer: 'Insurance appeal deadlines are typically 180 days from the date on the initial denial notice or EOB — but some plans allow only 60 or 90 days. Hospital billing dispute windows are often separate from insurance appeal deadlines. Do not wait to request your itemized bill and begin your review. The earlier you dispute, the more options you have. Disputing while a bill is still in the hospital\'s billing department — before it is sent to a collection agency — is significantly more effective.',
  },
